        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Downloads — put each file in the ComfyUI folder shown\n\n**Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1** — https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1\n\n| ComfyUI folder | File | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `models/diffusion_models/` | [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors) | 7.3 GB |\n| `models/text_encoders/` | [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors) | 9.4 GB |\n| `models/vae/` | [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors) | 0.68 GB |\n\n**Viggle/Qwen-Image-2.1-viggle-turbo** — only for the TURBO group — https://huggingface.co/Viggle/Qwen-Image-2.1-viggle-turbo\n\n| ComfyUI folder | File | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `models/loras/` | [Qwen-Image-2.1-viggle-turbo-v0.2.1-6step-lora-r256.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Viggle/Qwen-Image-2.1-viggle-turbo/resolve/main/Qwen-Image-2.1-viggle-turbo-v0.2.1-6step-lora-r256.safetensors) | 1.4 GB |\n\n**Needs ComfyUI 0.37 or newer** (native Qwen Image 2.1 + the Comfy Kitchen attention node). **No custom nodes.**\n\nOptional: `qwen_image_2.1_bf16.safetensors` (14.2 GB, same repo) is a drop-in swap for the int8 model. On my RTX 3060 at 2K it measured 6 min 10 s vs 3 min 57 s (25 steps) with 10.6 GB peak system RAM vs 3.0 GB — same-seed images looked the same.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Downloads",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -760,
        640
      ],
      "size": [
        720,
        760
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 21,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## How to use\n\n1. **Step 1** — models are set (int8 = best fit for 12 GB).\n2. **Step 2** — size. Default **4 MP = 2048×2048** (Qwen 2.1's native 2K). 1 MP = 1024×1024.\n3. **Step 3** — write your prompt. cfg stays **1** (negative prompt is unused at cfg 1).\n4. **Run.** QUALITY is on; TURBO is bypassed. To switch: click a group title → **Ctrl+B**.\n\n## Tested on RTX 3060 12 GB · Ryzen 5 5600X · 32 GB DDR4 (ComfyUI 0.37.1)\n\n| This workflow, 2048×2048 (Comfy Desktop, SageAttention on) | Time per image |\n|---|---|\n| QUALITY · 40 steps · Comfy Kitchen attention | **4 min 07 s** |\n| TURBO · Viggle 6-step · SageAttention (Desktop default) | **47 s** |\n\nFirst run after starting ComfyUI adds a few seconds for loading (4 min 11 s / 48 s).\n\nFrom my benchmark (2048×2048, same seed): template 25 steps with PyTorch attention **3 min 57 s** ·\nComfy Kitchen attention **2 min 40 s** · SageAttention **3 min 00 s** · bf16 model **6 min 10 s**.\n\n**Why 40 steps:** at 2K the template's 25 steps left the subject faded on one of my test prompts; 40 steps (the official 40–50) fixed it.\n**TURBO:** much faster, but visibly softer fine detail at 2K than the base model.\n**Seeds vary:** of my two test seeds, TURBO double-exposed the player's head on one, and QUALITY printed the date line twice on one. Re-roll the seed if you see that.\n**Don't add Comfy Kitchen attention to TURBO:** with the 6-step LoRA it ghosted the subject in my test — PyTorch and SageAttention were clean.\n**Text encoder:** `qwen3vl_8b_w4a8` runs at the same speed but changes the picture with the same seed — int8 kept.\n"
      ],
      "title": "How to use · tested on RTX 3060",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
